KZ3 patch 2037: keyboard and mouse buttons from a binding file, alongside an XInput pad (RSX pass 36 hook C;
configurable keybinds saved to a local config file). cellPad.c's one fixed keyboard table (patch 2034) is
replaced by keybinds.ini in the player's data folder (the install folder when kz3-install.ini next to the exe or
one level up says [install] portable = 1, else %APPDATA%\Project Helghast; KZ3_KEYBINDS=<path> overrides): one line
per pad input (16 buttons + both sticks as four directions each, diagonals by holding two keys), primary and
secondary key, mouse buttons Mouse1-5. Written with the defaults when missing, re-read when its time stamp changes
(checked every 2 s). Unknown inputs, unknown keys, extra keys and broken lines are logged ("[keybinds] line N: ...")
and ignored, never fatal. The keys are polled every time (not only when no XInput pad is on port 0) and merged into
port 0: buttons OR'ed, a held stick direction overrides that stick, L2/R2 keys give full triggers. PAD_NO_KEYBOARD=1
still turns the keyboard off. Parser, defaults and writer are platform-free in libs/input/pad_keybinds.h (host test
tools/smoke/test_pad_keybinds.sh). Upstream candidate (the table and the coexistence with a pad; KZ3's default
keys and data folder are port-specific).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): context only (upstream v0.18.0 changed lines around the hunks; same change).

